B.ai6=new A.b8(B.aGE,B.b5i,"The five daily prayers and when each is prayed:\n- Fajr (dawn): from true dawn, when the white thread of dawn shows, until sunrise.\n- Dhuhr (midday): from just after the sun passes its highest point until Asr begins.\n- Asr (afternoon): from when an object's shadow equals its height (Hanafi: twice its height) until sunset. The best time ends when the sun turns yellow.\n- Maghrib (sunset): from sunset until the red twilight has gone (the Hanafi school waits for the white twilight to go).\n- Isha (night): from the end of twilight until midnight, and by necessity until Fajr begins.\n\nThe Prophet \ufdfa said the time of Fajr lasts until the first part of the sun appears, Dhuhr until Asr comes, Asr until the sun turns yellow, Maghrib until the twilight disappears, and Isha until half the night has passed (Sahih Muslim 612). The Qur'an says \"prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times\" (Qur'an 4:103), and the white thread of dawn is in Qur'an 2:187.\n\nThe exact minutes for where you are depend on the calculation method. The Prayer Times screen shows today's times for your location, with alerts.\n\nSource: Sahih Muslim 612; Qur'an 4:103, 2:187.\n[GO:/prayer]",!0,"")
B.aXo=s(["\\bhow many\\b.*\\brakah\\b","\\bnumber of rakah\\b","\\brakah\\b.*\\b(?:in|of|for|is|are)\\b.*\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha|each|every|five|daily|fard|obligatory)\\b","\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b.*\\b(?:how many|rakah)\\b","\\bhow many (?:fard|obligatory|farz) (?:prayers?)\\b","\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b.*\\bsunnah\\b","\\bsunnah\\b.*\\b(?:fajr|dhuhr|asr|maghrib|isha)\\b","\\brawatib\\b","\\bsunnah (?:prayers?|rakah)\\b"],t.s)
B.b0g=s(["\\b(?:tahajj?ud|tahajud|qiyam|duha|ishraq|tarawee?h|istikhara|janazah|eid)\\b","\\b(?:app|screen)\\b"],t.s)
B.aio=new A.b8(B.aXo,B.b0g,"The five daily prayers have 17 obligatory (fard) rak'ahs: Fajr 2, Dhuhr 4, Asr 4, Maghrib 3, Isha 4. On Friday, Jumu'ah (2 rak'ahs with the khutbah) takes the place of Dhuhr. A traveller shortens the four-rak'ah prayers to 2.\n\nAlongside them are the regular sunnah prayers (rawatib). The Prophet \ufdfa promised a house in Paradise for twelve of them each day: four before Dhuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha and two before Fajr (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 415, sahih per Darussalam). The two before Fajr are the most emphasised. The schools differ on which are strongly emphasised and on extra ones (for example, four before Asr), so follow your school.\n\nWitr (odd rak'ahs after Isha) is separate; see the Witr guide.\n\nSource: Jami' at-Tirmidhi 415, sahih per Darussalam.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-nawafil]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-witr]",!0,"")
B.aIC=s(["\\bconditions? (?:of|for) (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bprerequisites? (?:of|for) (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bshurut\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|are) (?:needed|required) (?:for|before) (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bbefore (?:i |we )?(?:start|begin) (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bwhat makes (?:a |the )?prayers? (?:valid|accepted|sahih)\\b","\\bvalid(?:ity)? of (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bprayers? (?:conditions?|requirements?)\\b","\\bpillars? of (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bfard (?:acts )?of (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bwhat breaks (?:the |my )?prayers?\\b","\\bwhat invalidates (?:the |my )?prayers?\\b","\\bhow many (?:pillars?|fards?)\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bpillars? of salah\\b","\\bwhat nullif\\w+ (?:the )?prayers?\\b"],t.s)
B.ahi=new A.b8(B.aIC,B.c,"Before you pray, six conditions must be met:\n1. You are a Muslim, of sound mind, and past puberty (children are gently taught to pray from about seven, but it is not yet an obligation on them).\n2. The time of that prayer has begun. \"prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times\" (Qur'an 4:103).\n3. You are pure: wudu for the small impurity, ghusl for the big one. The Prophet \ufdfa said the prayer of someone who has broken wudu is not accepted until he makes wudu (Sahih al-Bukhari 135).\n4. Your body, clothes and prayer place are free of najasa (physical impurity).\n5. Your awrah is covered: for a man from the navel to the knee, for a woman her whole body except the face and hands (the Hanafi school also leaves the feet).\n6. You face the qibla and make the intention in your heart.\n\nInside the prayer, the pillars (without which it is not valid) are standing if you can, the opening takbir, reciting al-Fatihah, ruku', rising from it, sujud (twice in each rak'ah), the sitting between them, the last sitting with the tashahhud, blessings on the Prophet \ufdfa in it, and the salam. The schools count a few of these differently (for example, the Hanafi school treats the Fatihah as wajib, not a pillar), so ask your imam if you are unsure.\n\nWhat breaks the prayer: breaking wudu, speaking on purpose, a lot of unnecessary movement, eating or drinking, turning away from the qibla, laughing aloud, and leaving a pillar on purpose.\n\nSource: Qur'an 4:103; Sahih al-Bukhari 135.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-prayer]",!0,"")
B.b3z=s(["\\bfatiha\\b","\\balfatiha\\b","\\bopening (?:chapter|surah|of the book)\\b","\\bumm(?:ul)? (?:al )?(?:kitab|quran)\\b","\\b(?:minimum|least|smallest) .*\\brecit\\w*.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bwhat (?:do i|should i|to) recite\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\brecit\\w* (?:in|during) (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bwhich surah.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bhow much quran.*\\bprayers?\\b","\\bsurah.*\\bin (?:the )?prayers?\\b","\\bdo i have to recite\\b.*\\bprayers?\\b"],t.s)
