B.aiO=new A.b8(B.b3m,B.aQx,'The Games screen lists every game that works today, in four groups: Islamic (such as Qur\'an Knowledge, Stories Trivia, the 99 Names, Lineage Challenge and the Hijrah Journey), Strategy (Shatranj, which is chess), Family (Ludo) and Words and puzzles. Ask me about a game by name, for example "how do I play Ludo", and I will tell you the rules and how to start.\n\nScoring: the quizzes show how many you got right out of the total, and after each answer you see the source. There is no timer in the quizzes. Hints are free: a hint hides two wrong answers, and you get three free hints in a game. Nothing is sold, and there are no ratings, coins or leaderboards. Memorising the Qur\'an in Hifz practice has no score.\n\nA game you started and did not finish is shown at the top of the Games screen under "Continue playing". Finished games appear in Game history (button at the bottom of the Games screen), which is kept on this device only; you can clear it there. Playing Ludo or Shatranj with a friend on another device uses a six-letter code and needs the internet and the online hall to be switched on; if it is not, the app tells you.\n[GO:/games]\n[GO:/games/history]',!0,"")
B.b3B=s(["\\bdifference between\\b.*\\b(?:fard|farz|wajib|sunnah|nafl|mustahabb)\\b","\\b(?:fard|farz|wajib|mustahabb|nafl)\\b","\\bwhat (?:is|does) (?:fard|farz|wajib|sunnah mu?akkadah|makruh|mubah)\\b","\\bmeaning of (?:fard|farz|wajib|makruh|mubah|mustahabb|haram|halal)\\b","\\btypes? of (?:rulings?|actions?)\\b","\\bfive (?:categories|rulings)\\b","\\bwhat is (?:the )?(?:difference|meaning) .*\\bsunnah\\b.*\\bnafl\\b","\\bwhat (?:are|is) (?:the )?(?:categories|kinds|levels) of (?:ruling|obligation)\\b","\\bwhat does makruh mean\\b"],t.s)
B.aB3=s(["\\b(?:app|game)\\b"],t.s)
B.ahL=new A.b8(B.b3B,B.aB3,"Islamic law (fiqh) puts every action in one of these levels:\n- Fard (obligatory): required; reward for doing it, sin for leaving it. Examples: the five daily prayers, fasting Ramadan, zakat. A communal duty (fard kifayah) is one that is lifted from everyone once enough people do it, like the funeral prayer.\n- Wajib: in the Hanafi school, a duty just below fard (established by a text that is less certain), like witr and the Eid prayer; leaving it is sinful. The other schools treat wajib and fard as the same thing, except in Hajj.\n- Sunnah (recommended): what the Prophet \ufdfa did and encouraged; rewarded, and not sinful to leave. Sunnah mu'akkadah is a sunnah he rarely left, like the sunnah before Fajr.\n- Mustahabb / nafl (praiseworthy or voluntary): extra acts, rewarded, not emphasised.\n- Mubah (permitted): neither rewarded nor sinful.\n- Makruh (disliked): better to avoid; not sinful to do.\n- Haram (forbidden): sinful to do, rewarded to avoid for Allah's sake.\n\nNote that \"sunnah\" also means the whole way of the Prophet \ufdfa (his words, actions and approvals), which is the second source after the Qur'an.",!0,"")
